==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From the {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|hnot|lang=non}}. Cognates with the Latin {{term|nux|lang=la}}; Old English {{term|hnyt|lang=ang}} (English {{term|nut|lang=en}}; Old High German {{term|hnuz|lang=gho}} (German {{term|Nuss|lang=de}}); Danish {{term|nöd|lang=da}} and Swedish {{term|nöt|lagn=sv}}.

